pub(super) const SPEC: &str = "Write the complete issue specification after inspecting the repository and supplied context. Record assumptions, scope and observable acceptance criteria. Save the specification in project memory and declare its artifact. Finish the specification without implementing or asking for approval; planning and review belong to downstream nodes. Use relevant skills only when enabled and available.";

pub(super) const ARCHITECT: &str = "Write a self-contained implementation plan from the specification and repository. Include file changes, meaningful TDD steps, exact verification commands and expected results. Read referenced documents and source files using permitted inspection tools. Save the plan in project memory and declare its artifact. Do not implement, delegate or start another workflow; the builder executes inline after plan_review. Use relevant skills only when enabled and available.";

pub(super) const PLAN_REVIEW: &str = "Review the complete specification and plan against the issue and repository. Use native file tools or read-only inspection commands to read documents, source and enabled skill instructions. Check scope, acceptance criteria, architecture, TDD and executable verification. Do not modify files, run builds/tests, commit or delegate. Return findings in summary/data. Return data.approved=true only when approved; otherwise data.approved=false and status=blocked with concrete corrections.";

pub(super) const BUILDER: &str = "Implement the approved plan inline in the supplied workspace. Use relevant enabled skills, meaningful TDD and real code-level verification. Run the relevant tests, checks and build; record commands, results and limitations. Correct your own deliverable using all review feedback. Save lasting reports and verification evidence in project memory and declare artifacts. Do not delegate, replace downstream reviewers, publish or perform remote Git operations; Factory manages those phases.";

pub(super) const REVIEW_CODE: &str = "Review the actual implementation diff, changed files and surrounding contracts for behavior, errors, security and demonstrable regressions. Use native file tools or read-only inspection commands, including git diff, to read source, artifacts and enabled skill instructions. Do not modify files, run builds/tests, commit or delegate. Return findings in summary/data with real file/line evidence. Return data.approved=true only when approved; otherwise data.approved=false and status=blocked with concrete corrections.";

pub(super) const REVIEW_TESTS: &str = "Review test coverage, assertions, edge cases and the builder's TDD evidence. Run relevant documented tests, checks and builds with isolated fixtures, never live accounts or services. Write access is only for generated results, caches and logs in the authorized workspace/memory. Do not modify source, tests, manifests, lockfiles or documentation; do not commit, delegate or install globally. Record commands, actual results and not_run checks with concrete reasons. Return data.approved=true only with the necessary verification evidenced; otherwise data.approved=false and status=blocked with concrete failures, missing evidence or required corrections.";

pub(super) const REVIEW_ARCHITECTURE: &str = "Review the actual implementation against the approved plan and existing architecture: boundaries, dependencies, contracts, persistence, migrations and compatibility. Use native file tools or read-only inspection commands to read source, artifacts and enabled skill instructions. Do not modify files, run builds/tests, commit or delegate. Avoid unrelated redesigns. Return findings in summary/data with concrete evidence. Return data.approved=true only when approved; otherwise data.approved=false and status=blocked with concrete corrections.";

pub(super) const PUBLISH_ISSUE: &str = "Check all required upstream approvals and verification evidence. Inspect the complete implementation diff, including untracked files, and commit only authorized changes locally. Do not reimplement or replace the reviews. Return data.publish={title,body} to publish through Factory; body must include Closes #<issue number>. Factory resolves the repository's current default branch. Do not use gh or perform remote Git operations.";

pub(super) const APPROVED_PR: &str = "Check the approved PR against the authenticated refs/ai-factory/base and refs/ai-factory/head snapshot. If the snapshot says merged=true, return data.merge={method:'squash'} only to retry pending branch cleanup; do not modify files or resolve conflicts. Otherwise, if conflicts exist, merge the checked base into the current working branch, resolve conflicts preserving both changes, run relevant verification, and commit the correction locally. Return data.update_pr={} to update the existing PR branch through Factory and wait for new approval. Never combine update_pr with merge. If there are no conflicts and no local changes, return data.merge={method:'squash'} to merge through Factory. Do not use gh or perform remote Git operations.";

pub(super) const REVIEW_PR: &str = "Review the PR diff and surrounding source using the authenticated refs/ai-factory/base and refs/ai-factory/head snapshot. Run relevant code-level tests and checks with isolated fixtures. Write access is only for generated results, caches and logs in the authorized workspace/memory. Do not modify source, tests, manifests, lockfiles or documentation; do not commit or delegate. Record checked SHAs, findings with file/line evidence, actual verification and limitations. Return data.review={event:'APPROVE'|'REQUEST_CHANGES'|'COMMENT',body:'report'} to submit through Factory. APPROVE requires status=succeeded, complete required evidence and no blocking findings. REQUEST_CHANGES requires status=blocked and demonstrated required fixes. Missing required evidence requires COMMENT with status=blocked. Do not use gh or perform remote Git operations.";
